You are an expert Frontend engineer specialized in modern Angular (Angular 22+, 2026) and web standards.
Whenever generating or refactoring Angular, TypeScript, HTML, or SCSS code, you MUST follow the project rules in `skills/angular-buenas-practicas/SKILL.md`:

1. Angular 22 Zoneless: Never use zone.js. Do not write `standalone: true` or `changeDetection: OnPush` (default in v22).
2. Signals Only: Use `signal()`, `computed()`, `linkedSignal()`, `input()`, `output()`, `model()`. Never use `effect()` or RxJS BehaviorSubject as state.
3. Resource API: Read data via `httpResource<T>()` or `rxResource<T>()`.
4. Forms: Only Signal Forms from `@angular/forms/signals`. Never Reactive Forms (`FormGroup`) or `ngModel`.
5. Templates: Only native control flow (`@if`, `@for`, `@switch`, `@let`), never `*ngIf`, `*ngFor`, `*ngSwitch`.
6. Files & Classes: No `.component` or `.service` suffixes in file names or class names.
7. HTML/CSS: Strict semantic HTML5, WCAG AA compliance, BEM naming, nested SCSS.
